.TH "GLESHA-CONFIGURE" "1" "" "glesha" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
glesha-configure \- change a set's saved settings or map imported roots
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B glesha configure SET [options]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Change a set's saved settings or map imported roots. Previously bound source paths cannot be replaced.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-chunked
Use independent encrypted chunks with bounded local spool space. \-\-chunked=false selects a single archive.
.TP
.B \-\-spool\-max SIZE
Maximum chunk spool space (default 128MiB); accepts 128M, 1.1G and binary MiB/GiB units.
.TP
.B \-\-L STRING
debug, info, warn, error or silent (default "info")
.TP
.B \-\-baseline STRING
explicit snapshot baseline
.TP
.B \-\-catalog\-to STRING
catalog remote or local
.TP
.B \-\-color STRING
yes, no or auto; always/never aliases accepted (default "auto")
.TP
.B \-\-compression STRING
xz, gzip or bzip2
.TP
.B \-\-compression\-level INT
compression level 1..9
.TP
.B \-\-config STRING
TOML configuration file
.TP
.B \-\-env STRING
explicit credential environment file
.TP
.B \-\-h
show help
.TP
.B \-\-help
show help
.TP
.B \-\-incremental\-storage\-class STRING
AWS incremental storage class
.TP
.B \-\-json
versioned JSON output
.TP
.B \-\-log\-level STRING
debug, info, warn, error or silent (default "info")
.TP
.B \-\-prefix STRING
glesha or encb
.TP
.B \-\-root VALUE
archive root NAME=source PATH
.TP
.B \-\-storage\-class STRING
AWS storage class
.TP
.B \-\-to VALUE
remote names; comma\-separated or repeated
.TP
.B \-\-version
show version; \-version is also accepted.
.TP
.B \-v
Alias for \-\-version.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
glesha configure docs \-\-compression gzip

glesha configure imported \-\-root Documents=~/Documents \-\-to b2 \-\-catalog\-to b2
.fi
.SH OUTPUT
Colors default to auto: enabled only on a terminal. Use --color=yes to force colors,
or --color=no to disable them. The earlier always and never names remain aliases.
Interactive stderr displays a progress bar, readable byte counts and average speed.
Progress is disabled for redirected stderr, JSON output and warn/error/silent logging.
Scanning uses an ASCII spinner (minus, backslash, vertical bar, slash).
Archiving shows processed/total uncompressed file bytes and a percentage.
Finalization and metadata publication show status without an indefinite bar. Bars refresh every 100 ms, use # for filled
progress and adapt to about 80 percent of terminal width. Upload progress includes
in-flight payload bytes; checksum reads and retries do not count bytes twice. Bytes reaching 100 percent do not imply
that final validation or catalog publication has finished.
Use --log-level=debug for operation and worker-budget diagnostics.
Progress counters use compact binary units: [63.35%] [1.27G/2.34G] [1.22M/s].
Explicit worker flags show the effective worker count; archiving and individual
downloads use one worker. Other human sizes use KiB, MiB and GiB. JSON retains integer byte counts.
.SH COMPATIBILITY
Existing encb gzip/OpenPGP archives are read without recompression or replacement.
Compression is detected from the decrypted stream, independent of filenames.
Passwords are never stored. Archive passwords and the catalog secret are separate.
Database and JSON formats are versioned. Unsupported catalog schemas are rejected
without modifying the file; old catalogs are neither migrated nor deleted implicitly.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0: success. 1: operation failure. 2: invalid usage or missing selection.
3: pending work or cold retrieval. 4: conflicting remote history.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR glesha (1),
.BR glesha-help (1)
